    "title": "Power outages impact almost 37K across NEPA after storms - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julia Priest ,\n2 hours ago\n(WBRE/WYOU) — After winds and rain passed through Pennsylvania, thousands of members of the commonwealth experienced power outages on Wednesday night.\nAs of about 9:30 p.m., almost 37,000 PPL customers in our coverage area were experiencing power outages.\nWeather Alert: NWS issues thunderstorm warnings, wind advisories Of that number, over 12,000 were reported in Wayne County, according to PPL .\nMeanwhile, Claverack Rural Electric Cooperative is reporting that over 6,000 customers were impacted on Wednesday night.\nTo stay up to date on the latest weather alerts , use the 28/22 News Interactive Radar .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n3",
